WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.770
Speaker 1: This is just an unbelievable story.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:10.700
After months and months of wrangling, trying
to avoid providing call records to the House

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.630
Committee investigating the Jan. six Trump
riots.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:20.780
The Trump White House, the former White House,
finally provided the call records to the January

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:21.780
6th Committee.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.780
Great.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:23.780
Right?

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.780
I mean, what delightful?

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.720
They've got the information they need.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:33.300
No, the January six call logs provided by
Trump to the committee.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:42.910
Have a seven hour gap on January 6th, the
key hours during which it is crucial and critical

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.969
to understand who was Trump speaking to.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:51.170
Now there's a second layer to this, which
is they may have had phone calls that they

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.550
never put in the log.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.579
So there's kind of two layers of accountability.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:00:58.219
The first is give us the logs so we can see
who you spoke to.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:00.850
That assumes the logs are accurate.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.449
And I would not assume that with this former
administration.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:09.530
But the next part of it is, of course, well,
do the calls even reflect what what they should

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.759
reflect?

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:15.969
Washington Post report Very good report by
Bob Woodward and Robert Costa.

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:21.399
January six White House logs given to the
House show a seven hour gap.

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:22.909
Wow.

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:27.289
The House Select Committee is now investigating
whether it has the full record and whether

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:32.649
Trump communicated that day through back channels,
phones of aides or personal disposable phones.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:35.649
Now Trump is claiming he doesn't know what
a burner phone is.

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:36.929
I don't believe that for a second.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:39.029
We're going to get to that in a moment.

00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:41.380
Read the whole article we're linking to it.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.109
Internal White House records from the day
of the attack that were turned over to the

00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:50.789
House Select Committee show a gap in Trump's
phone logs of seven hours and 37 minutes,

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:53.020
including what a surprise.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.149
The period when the building was being violently
assaulted, according to documents obtained

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.669
by The Washington Post and CBS News.

00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:06.450
The lack of an official White House notation
of any calls placed to or by Trump for 457

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:13.470
minutes look at the time here from 11:17 a.m.
to 6:54 pm trying to think what was going

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.769
on during that time.

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:15.769
Oh, right.

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:21.450
That was exactly when the Capitol was taken
over by violent insurrectionists attempting

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.890
to overturn the results of the election.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.280
Well, during that time, we don't have the
logs.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.459
That means the committee has no record of
his phone conversations as his supporters

00:02:31.459 --> 00:02:37.040
descended on the Capitol, battled overwhelmed
police and forcibly entered the building,

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.959
prompting lawmakers and VP Mike Pence to flee
for safety.

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:45.400
The 11 pages of records, which consist of
the president's official daily diary and the

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.769
White House switchboard call logs, were turned
over by the National Archives earlier this

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.769
year.

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:55.120
The records show Trump was active on the phone
for part of the day, documenting conversations

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.390
with at least eight people in the morning
and 11 in the evening.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:04.040
But there is this seven hour gap that stands
in stark contrast to the extensive public

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.519
reporting about phone calls he had with allies
during the attack.

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:08.999
We know he spoke to Mike Lee.

00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:11.099
He spoke to Tommy Tuberville.

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:13.849
He spoke to Kevin McCarthy and many others.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:21.659
So in essence, they didn't really turn over
the records in that we don't actually have

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:27.079
the records or the White House doesn't during
those key moments.

00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:29.819
Now I want to talk about this burner thing.

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:31.870
This is now from a CBS News article.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:37.260
Remember that this was a kind of joint report
from Washington Post and CBS.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.640
The House panel is now investigating whether
Trump communicated through back channels,

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.860
meaning he could have used other people's
phones or personal disposable phones known

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.790
as burner phones.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.790
Look at this.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:55.190
In a statement Monday night, Trump said, I
have no idea what a burner phone is.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:00.590
To the best of my knowledge, I have never
even heard the term.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:06.280
Does anybody believe that, does anybody believe
that Donald Trump doesn't know what a burner

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.330
phone is?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:14.140
I know he's not the brightest, but there is
no doubt that he knows what a burner phone

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:18.870
is, the stuff that Trump has been up to for
so long now.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.489
Is it possible he doesn't know it by that
name?

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:25.110
He knows it as a disposable phone.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:30.960
I don't know, guys, maybe, maybe, but this
is not believable.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.660
And when we talk about.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.789
Remember when we spoke about the Ukraine fiasco
that led to the second impeachment?

00:04:38.789 --> 00:04:44.460
Remember when we spoke about the entire Russia
probe, quite frankly, as I've said before,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.600
if from the beginning of the suspicions about
Russia, the Mueller investigation, the entire

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
thing.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.860
Much of what took place was self-inflicted
harm done by Trump.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:00.120
If Trump hadn't gone public and tweeted all
sorts of things that attracted more attention

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:05.620
to the story, if Trump hadn't gone overboard
in his denials and then it came out, actually,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.479
they met with all of these Russian individuals
and all these different things.

00:05:10.479 --> 00:05:13.610
The investigation would never have become
what it was.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:20.920
And similarly, when it comes to January six,
it is increasingly plausible that had Trump

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:26.300
just cooperated and not called attention to
the fact that he's obviously trying to cover

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.139
up the full scope of what he did and what
he said and who he spoke to that day.

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:36.720
This also likely would not be as big as it
is because, to be perfectly frank, my opinion

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:43.410
is whatever is in those missing seven and
a half hours, it's probably not good.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:49.810
But if you don't have the contents of those
calls, you have a circumstantial case at best,

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.180
most likely.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.090
And again, the fact that there is a seven
and a half hour gap in the records at exactly

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.840
the key time that's being investigated is
just putting more of a focus on that time

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.830
and suggesting that Donald Trump knows that
he did something wrong.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.280
So I'm not suggesting Trump is innocent.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:13.039
But what I am suggesting is that the cover
up after the fact, the actions are putting

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:17.479
more of a spotlight when you don't give seven
and a half hours of logs.

00:06:17.479 --> 00:06:20.639
You're saying these are the seven and a half
hours that you want to focus on.

00:06:20.639 --> 00:06:25.960
Now, unfortunately, and I know we continue
to have this discussion, you and I in the

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.380
audience.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.310
It's not looking to me like there are going
to be any consequences here.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:35.240
Number one, there seems to be no willingness
on the part of any prosecutor to actually

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.509
look at criminal charges for any of what's
taking place.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:41.229
And no, to listen.

00:06:41.229 --> 00:06:42.990
Trump is pretty Teflon.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:47.590
It's just the reality, and he's thinking about
running again in 2024.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:52.940
There's the possibility that even running
again may be part of keeping himself out of

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.442
trouble, trouble by being back in power.

00:06:54.442 --> 00:07:02.699
And I remain pessimistic about accountability
here, but in the last 24 hours, just incredible

00:07:02.699 --> 00:07:07.780
stories and a seven and a half hour gap in
the phone records.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.290
If you believe that we are finally getting
to where it's overwhelming.

